#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate Scottland (Wayfire) shortcuts from the user's live Omarchy Hyprland config.

Called by start-scottland with the base Wayfire config as its argument; prints an ini fragment
that start-scottland appends. Runs every session start, so Hyprland shortcut changes carry over.

  - Shortcuts that run commands (menus, apps, media keys, screenshots, toggles) are kept.
  - Shortcuts that Scottland does not use (window navigation, layout, workspaces, groups) or
    cannot translate are skipped and listed in the fragment's comments and grouped report.
  - Where one clashes with another default, the Omarchy shortcut usually wins; Scottland feature
    keys and key_remaps combos are reserved for Scottland and listed as displaced.

The report is saved at ~/.local/state/scottland/omarchy-overrides.txt and opened only when its
content has not been shown before. Setup opens it once; startup defers a pending report until the
compositor and shim are running. Omarchy's default coding agent is preferred, with the editor as
fallback.

The Lua scan follows omarchy-menu-keybindings: the config runs against a stand-in `hl` that
records binds instead of applying them. This one also honours hl.unbind.
"""

import fcntl
import hashlib
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
